"3413",""
"3414","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to a woman from a people called Sawdah. She was a woman with children from a previous marriage (musbiyah), having five or six children from a husband of hers who had died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: ""What prevents you from me?"" She said: ""By Allah, O Prophet of Allah! Nothing prevents me from you except that you are not the most beloved of creation to me, but I honor you lest these children press against your head morning and evening."" He said: ""Is there anything other than that preventing you from me?"" She said: ""No, by Allah!"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: ""May Allah have mercy on you. Indeed, the best women who rode camel saddles are the righteous women of Quraysh: the most compassionate toward a child in infancy, and the most attentive to a husband with what she possesses."""
"3415","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Satirize the Quraysh, for it is more severe upon them than a volley of arrows."" So he sent for Ibn Rawāḥah and said: ""Satirize them."" He satirized them, but it did not please him. Then he sent for Kaʿb ibn Mālik, then he sent for Ḥassān ibn Thābit. When he entered upon him, Ḥassān said: ""It is time for you to send for this lion who strikes with his tail."" Then he stuck out his tongue and began moving it, saying: ""By Him Who sent you with the truth, I shall strip them with my tongue as leather is stripped."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Do not hasten, for Abū Bakr knows the Quraysh better than anyone regarding their lineages, and I have lineage among them; let him clarify my lineage for you."" So Ḥassān went to him, then returned and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! He has clarified your lineage for me, and by Him Who sent you with the truth, I shall extract you from them as a hair is extracted from dough."" ʿĀʾishah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying to Ḥassān: ""The Holy Spirit will not cease to support you as long as you defend Allah and His Messenger."" And she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: ""Ḥassān satirized them, so he healed and was healed.""Ḥassān said:You satirized Muḥammad, so I answered on his behalf,And with Allah, in that, is the reward.You satirized Muḥammad, a righteous, upright man,The Messenger of Allah, whose character is fidelity.For my father and his father and my honorAre a protection for the honor of Muḥammad from you.May I lose my little daughter if you do not see herStirring up dust from the sides of Kadāʾ,Our mares crossing the reins, ascending,Upon their shoulders are the thirsty, polished spears.Our steeds remain rain-drenched,While women strike them with their veils.If you turn away from us, we shall perform ʿUmrah,And victory shall come and the cover shall be removed.But if not, then be patient for the striking of a dayIn which Allah honors whom He wills.And Allah said: ""I have sent a servantWho speaks the truth, there is no ambiguity in him.""And Allah said: ""I have facilitated a host—They are the Anṣār, their nature is encounter.""For us, on every day from Maʿadd,Is reviling or fighting or satire.So whoever among you satirizes the Messenger of Allah,And praises him and supports him—it is all the same.And Jibrīl is the Messenger of Allah among us,And the Holy Spirit—there is no equal for him."
"3416",""
"3417",""
"3418",""
"3419","On the authority of Zayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿīd ibn ʿAmr ibn Nufayl of Banū ʿAdī, from his father, who said: I came to Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī accompanied by a group of young men from Quraysh. We entered upon him after his eyesight had failed. We found a rope hanging from the ceiling and loaves of bread placed before him. Whenever a poor person asked for food, Jābir would stand up, take a loaf, hold the rope until he reached the poor person to give it to him, then return by the rope until he sat down. I said to him: ""May Allah grant you well-being. We, when a poor person comes, we give [to him]."" He said: ""I anticipate reward for the walking in this."" Then he said: ""Shall I not inform you of something I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" They said: ""Yes."" He said: ""I heard him say: 'Indeed, Quraysh are people of trustworthiness; no one seeks to undermine them with stumbling blocks except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will throw him down on his nose.'"""
"3420","'Amr ibn Salamah al-Hamdani said: We used to sit at the door of 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud before the Fajr prayer. When he came out, we would walk with him to the mosque. Abu Musa al-Ash'ari came to us and said: ""Has Abu 'Abd al-Rahman come out to you yet?"" We said: ""No."" So he sat with us until he came out. When he came out, we all stood up to him. Abu Musa said to him: ""O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman! I saw something in the mosque just now that I disapproved of, and I saw nothing, praise be to Allah, but good."" He said: ""What is it?"" He said: ""If you live, you will see it."" He said: ""I saw in the mosque people sitting in circles waiting for the prayer. In each circle there was a man, and in their hands were pebbles. He would say: 'Say Allahu Akbar one hundred times,' and they would say Allahu Akbar one hundred times. Then he would say: 'Say La ilaha illa Allah one hundred times,' and they would say La ilaha illa Allah one hundred times. And he would say: 'Say Subhan Allah one hundred times,' and they would say Subhan Allah one hundred times."" He said: ""What did you say to them?"" He said: ""I did not say anything to them, waiting for your opinion."" He said: ""Why did you not order them to count their evil deeds and guarantee them that nothing of their good deeds would be lost?"" Then he went on, and we went with him until he came to one of those circles. He stood over them and said: ""What is this that I see you doing?"" They said: ""O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman! These are pebbles with which we count the takbir, tahlil, and tasbih."" He said: ""Count your evil deeds, for I guarantee that nothing of your good deeds will be lost. Woe to you, O Ummah of Muhammad! How quickly you go to ruin! These are the Companions of your Prophet ﷺ still abundant, and these are his garments not yet worn out, and his vessels not yet broken. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! You are either on a religion better guided than the religion of Muhammad, or you are opening a door of misguidance."" They said: ""By Allah! O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman! We intended nothing but good."" He said: ""And how many are those who intend good but do not achieve it. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us: 'A people will recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will pass through Islam as an arrow passes through the target.' And by Allah! I do not know, perhaps most of them are from you."" Then he turned away from them. 'Amr ibn Salamah said: We saw most of those circles fighting against us on the Day of Nahrawan along with the Khawarij."
"3421","Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated from his father that a black slave woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) when he returned from one of his military expeditions. She said: ""I had vowed that if Allah returned you safely, I would beat the duff (tambourine) in your presence."" He said: ""If you did so, then do it; and if you did not, then do not do it."" So she beat it. Then Abu Bakr entered while she was beating it, and others entered while she was beating it. Then Umar entered, and she put her duff behind her back while she was veiled. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Satan flees from you, O Umar! I was sitting here and these people entered, but when you entered, she did what she did."""
"3422",""
"3423",""
"3424",""
"3425","Ibn Abbas said: The leaders of Quraysh gathered in the Hijr and made a pact by Al-Lat, Al-Uzza, Manat the third, the other, and Naila and Isaf: ""If we see Muhammad, we will surely rise against him as one man and not leave him until we kill him."" Then his daughter Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) came weeping until she entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: ""These leaders of Quraysh have made a pact against you; if they see you, they will surely rise against you and kill you. There is not a man among them except that he has known his share of your blood."" He said: ""O my daughter! Bring me water for ablution."" So he performed ablution, then entered the mosque upon them. When they saw him, they said: ""Here he is."" And they lowered their gazes, their chins fell upon their chests, and they were rooted in their seats. None of them raised their gaze to him, and no man among them rose against him. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) approached until he stood over their heads, took a handful of dust, and said: ""May the faces be humiliated."" Then he threw it at them. No man among them was struck by a pebble from that dust except he was killed on the day of Badr as a disbeliever."
"3426",""
"3427",""
"3428",""
"3429",""
"3430",""
"3431",""
"3432","On the authority of ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from a man of the Anṣār, that Anas al-Anṣārī informed ʿAṭāʾ that he kissed his wife during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) while he was fasting. So he ordered his wife to ask the Prophet (peace be upon him) about that. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed the Messenger of Allah does that."" His wife informed him, so he said: ""Indeed the Prophet (peace be upon him) has concessions in some matters. Go back to him and say to him."" She returned to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: ""He says: Indeed the Prophet (peace be upon him) has concessions in some matters."" He said: ""I am the most God-fearing of you for Allah and the most knowledgeable of you regarding the limits of Allah."""
"3433",""
"3434",""
"3435",""
"3436",""
"3437",""
"3438",""
"3439","On the authority of Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith, she said: While I was passing by, the Prophet ﷺ was in the Hijr. He said: ""O Umm al-Fadl!"" I replied: ""At your service, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""You are pregnant with a male child."" She said: ""How can that be, when Quraysh have sworn an oath not to give birth to females?"" He said: ""It is as I say to you. When you deliver him, bring him to me."" When she gave birth, she brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. He named him Abdullah, and performed tahneek for him with his saliva. Then he said: ""Take him, for you will find him to be sagacious."" She said: ""I went to al-Abbas and informed him. He dressed up and came to the Prophet ﷺ. He was a handsome man, tall in stature. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him, he stood up for him, kissed him between the eyes, and seated him on his right. Then he said: 'This is my uncle. Whoever wishes may boast of his uncle.' Al-Abbas said: 'Some of the speech, O Messenger of Allah!' He replied: 'Why should I not say it, when you are my uncle and the remnant of my forefathers, and the uncle is like a father.'"""
"3440",""
"3441",""
"3442",""
"3443","On the authority of Amr ibn Abasah: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Who has followed you in this matter?"" He said: ""A free man and a slave."" I said: ""What is Islam?"" He said: ""Good speech and feeding food."" I said: ""What is faith (Iman)?"" He said: ""Patience and generosity."" I said: ""Which Islam is best?"" He said: ""He from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."" I said: ""Which faith is best?"" He said: ""Good character."" I said: ""Which prayer is best?"" He said: ""Length of standing (in prayer)."" I said: ""Which migration is best?"" He said: ""That you abandon what your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, dislikes."" I said: ""Then which jihad is best?"" He said: ""He whose mount is hamstrung and his blood is shed."" I said: ""Which hour is best?"" He said: ""The middle of the last part of the night..."""
"3444",""
"3445","Sa'id ibn al-'As reported that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ (Muslim and others added: ""and Uthman""), narrated to him that Abu Bakr sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reclining on his bed wearing Aisha's mantle. So he permitted Abu Bakr while he was in that state, and he fulfilled his need with him, then he left. Then Umar sought permission, so he permitted him while he was in that same state, and he fulfilled his need with him, then he left. Uthman said: ""Then I sought permission to enter upon him, so he sat up and said to Aisha: 'Gather your clothes upon yourself.' So I fulfilled my need with him, then I left."" Aisha said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Why did I not see you startled for Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, as you were startled for Uthman?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Indeed, Uthman is a man of modesty, and I feared that if I permitted him in that state, he would not convey his need to me."""
"3446",""
"3447","On the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās, he said: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb say: When ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy died, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was invited to pray over him. He stood up to do so. When he stood over him intending to pray, I moved until I stood at his chest and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! [Will you pray] over the enemy of Allah, ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy, who said on such-and-such day such-and-such?"" — enumerating his days. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) kept smiling until I spoke excessively. He said: ""Leave me alone, O ʿUmar. I have been given the choice and I chose. It was said to me: [Quran 9:80] 'Whether you ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them — even if you ask forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah will never forgive them.' If I knew that if I increased beyond seventy he would be forgiven, I would have increased."" Then he prayed over him and walked with him, and stood at his grave until he was finished. He said: I was amazed at myself and my boldness toward the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), but Allah and His Messenger know best. By Allah, it was only a short time until these two verses were revealed: [Quran 9:84] ""And do not pray over any of them who has died ever, nor stand at his grave. Indeed, they disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger and died while they were defiantly disobedient."" Until the end of the verse. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never prayed over a hypocrite after him, nor stood at his grave, until Allah took him."
"3448",""
"3449",""
"3450",""
"3451",""
"3452",""
"3453",""
"3454",""
"3455",""
"3456",""
"3457","From Abu Fakhita, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited us and stayed overnight with us, and Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn were sleeping. Al-Hasan asked for water, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up to a water skin of ours and squeezed it into a cup, then gave him to drink. Al-Husayn reached out to drink, but he prevented him and started with Al-Hasan. Fatima said: O Messenger of Allah! It seems as if he is more beloved to you. He said: No, but he asked for water first. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Indeed, I and you, and these two, and this sleeping one — meaning Ali — will be in one place on the Day of Resurrection. That is, Fatima and her two sons: Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn."
"3458","Amr ibn Abi Qurra said: Hudhayfah was in al-Mada'in, and he would narrate things that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to some of his companions in anger. People who heard this from Hudhayfah would go to Salman and tell him Hudhayfah's statement. Salman would say: ""Hudhayfah knows best what he says."" They would return to Hudhayfah and say: ""We mentioned your statement to Salman, and he neither confirmed you nor denied you."" So Hudhayfah came to Salman while he was in a date-drying place (mabqala) and said: ""O Salman! What prevents you from confirming me regarding what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" Salman said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would become angry and say things in his anger to some of his companions, and he would become pleased and say things in his pleasure to some of his companions. Will you not stop until you make men love men and hate men, and until you cause disagreement and division? And you certainly know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon and said: 'Any man of my nation whom I insulted with an insult or cursed with a curse in my anger - for I am only a son of Adam, I get angry as they get angry, and I was only sent as a mercy to the worlds - so make it a prayer for them on the Day of Resurrection.' By Allah, you will certainly stop, or I will write to Umar."""
"3459","Muhammad ibn Sa'd narrated from his father who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and with him were women from Quraysh asking him and requesting more from him, their voices raised above his voice. When Umar sought permission, they hurried to the hijab. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) gave him permission, so he entered while the Prophet (peace be upon him) was laughing. He said: ""May Allah keep your teeth laughing, O Messenger of Allah! May my father and mother be sacrificed for you."" He said: ""I am amazed at these women who were with me; when they heard your voice, they hurried to the hijab."" He said: ""You are more deserving that they fear you, O Messenger of Allah."" Then he turned to them and said: ""O enemies of yourselves! You fear me but you do not fear the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)?"" They said: ""You are harsher and sterner than the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Ah, O son of al-Khattab! By Him in Whose Hand is my soul! The devil never meets you traveling a path but he takes a path other than yours."""
"3460",""
"3461",""
"3462",""
"3463",""
"3464",""
"3465",""
"3466","On the authority of Abū Umāmah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to my people, (the tribe of) Bahilah. (I reached them while I was hungry.) I came upon them while they were eating food, (and in another narration: they were eating blood). They brought me back with them and honored me. They said: ""Welcome, O al-Ṣudayy ibn ʿAjlān!"" They said: ""We have heard that you have apostatized to this man."" I said: ""No, but I have believed in Allah and His Messenger, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to you to present to you Islam and its laws."" They said: ""Come, eat."" I said: ""(Woe to you! Verily) I have only come to forbid you from this, and I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; I have come to you that you may believe in him."" (So I began calling them to Islam.) They denied me and reviled me. I said to them: ""Woe to you! Bring me some water, for I am severely thirsty."" He said: ""And I had my turban on me."" They said: ""No, but we will leave you to die of thirst."" So I departed, hungry and thirsty, with severe exhaustion having befallen me. He said: So I wrapped my turban, laid my head in the turban, and slept on the hot sand in intense heat. Then in my sleep I was brought a draught of milk, the like of which people have never seen more delicious. He enabled me to drink it, so I drank, was satiated, and my belly swelled. The people said: ""A man from the best and noblest of you came to you, and you rejected him. Go to him and feed him whatever food and drink he desires."" They brought me food. I said: ""I have no need for your food or drink, for Allah has fed me and given me drink."" They looked at the state I was in. I showed them my belly, they looked, and they believed in me and in what I brought from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, (and they all embraced Islam)."
"3467","On the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn Najiyy, from his father, who said: I traveled with ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), and I was the carrier of his water vessel. When we passed by Nineveh while he was on his way to Ṣiffīn, ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) called out: ""Be patient, Abū ʿAbdullāh! Be patient, Abū ʿAbdullāh, by the bank of the Euphrates!"" I said: ""And what is that?"" He said: ""I entered upon the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) one day, and his eyes were overflowing with tears. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has someone angered you? Why are your eyes overflowing?' He said: 'Rather, Gabriel came to me just now and informed me that al-Ḥusayn will be killed by the bank of the Euphrates.' He said: 'Would you like me to let you smell his soil?' I said: 'Yes.' So he extended his hand, took a handful of dust, and gave it to me, and I could not prevent my eyes from overflowing."""
"3468",""
"3469",""
"3470",""
"3471",""
"3472","On the authority of Al-Barā' ibn 'Āzib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached, and it was said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Indeed Abū Sufyān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn 'Abd al-Muṭṭalib satirizes you."" So Ibn Rawāḥah stood up and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Permit me to deal with him."" He said: ""Are you the one who says 'Allah has made firm'?"" He said: ""Yes."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah: So may Allah make firm what He gave you of the good firmness of Mūsā and a victory like their victory."" He said: ""And you, may Allah do good to you similarly."" Then Ka'b jumped up and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Permit me to deal with him."" He said: ""Are you the one who says 'She intended'?"" He said: ""Yes."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah: Sakīnah intended to contend with her Lord, so the Contender of contenders will surely overcome."" He said: ""Indeed Allah has not forgotten that for you."" Then Ḥassān stood up and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Permit me to deal with him,"" and he stuck out a black tongue for him. He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Permit me, if you wish I will pierce the water-skin with it."" He said: ""Go to Abū Bakr so he may inform you of the news of the people and their days and their lineages, then satirize them, and Jibrīl is with you."""
"3473",""
"3474","Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: My father ordered me to prepare a khazīrah, so I prepared it. Then he ordered me to take it to the Prophet ﷺ. I came to him while he was in his house. He said to me: ""What do you have with you, O Jābir, is it meat?"" I said: ""No."" So I went back to my father, and he said to me: ""Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Then why did you not hear him say something?"" I said: ""Yes, he said: 'What do you have with you, O Jābir, is it meat?'"" He thought perhaps the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a desire for it, so he ordered a domesticated sheep of ours to be slaughtered, then ordered it to be roasted, then ordered me to take it to the Prophet ﷺ. He said to me: ""What do you have with you, O Jābir?"" I informed him, so he said: ""May Allah reward the Anṣār on our behalf with good, especially ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥarām and Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah."""
"3475",""
"3476",""
"3477",""
"3478",""
"3479",""
"3480","On the authority of Abu Nadrah, from Abdullah ibn Mawalah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: While I was traveling in Al-Ahwaz, I encountered a man riding ahead of me on a mule or a female mule. He was supplicating: ""O Allah, my generation from this ummah has passed away, so join me with them."" I said: ""And I as well, so include me in your supplication."" He said: ""And this companion of mine, if he wishes that."" Then he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'The best of my ummah is my generation, then those who follow them.'"" He said: ""And I do not know whether he mentioned the third or not."" Then he said: ""Then there will come after them a people among whom obesity will appear; they will give testimony without being asked for it."" He said: ""And behold, it was Buraydah al-Aslami."""
