"3499","On the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""I saw in a dream as if I were in a secure coat of armor, and I saw cows slaughtered. So I interpreted the secure coat of armor as Medina, and the cows — by Allah! — as good (martyrdom)."" He said: So he said to his companions: ""If we stay in Medina, then if they enter upon us therein, we will fight them."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! By Allah! We were not entered upon therein during the pre-Islamic period, so how would we be entered upon therein in Islam?"" 'Affan said in his narration: So he said: ""Your affair then."" He said: So he put on his armor. He said: So the Ansar said: ""We have returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) his opinion."" So they came and said: ""O Prophet of Allah! Your affair then."" He said: ""It is not for a prophet, when he has put on his armor, to take it off until he fights."""
