"3541","On the authority of ʿAmr ibn ʿAbasa al-Sulamī, who said: One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was reviewing horses, and ʿUyayna ibn Ḥiṣn ibn Badr al-Fazārī was with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: ""I am more knowledgeable about horses than you."" ʿUyayna said: ""And I am more knowledgeable about men than you."" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: ""How so?"" He said: ""The best of men are men who carry their swords on their shoulders, placing their spears on the saddles of their horses, wearing cloaks, from the people of Najd."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""You have lied. Rather, the best of men are the men of the people of Yemen. Faith is Yemeni, extending to Lakhm, Judhām, and ʿĀmila. The consumed of Ḥimyar is better than its consumer, and Ḥaḍramawt is better than Banū al-Ḥārith. Tribe is better than tribe, and tribe is worse than tribe. By Allah! I do not care if the two Ḥāriths both perish. May Allah curse the four kings: Jamdāʾ, Mikhwisāʾ, Mushrakhāʾ, Abḍaʿa, and their sister al-ʿAmarrada."" Then he said: ""My Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to curse Quraysh twice, so I cursed them; and He commanded me to pray for them, so I prayed for them twice."" Then he said: ""ʿUṣayya disobeyed Allah and His Messenger, except Qays, Jaʿda, and ʿUṣayya."" Then he said: ""Aslam, Ghifār, Muzayna, and their allies from Juhayna are better than Banū Asad, Tamīm, Ghaṭafān, and Hawāzin in the sight of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection."" Then he said: ""The worst two tribes among the Arabs are Najrān and Banū Taghlib, and the most tribes in Paradise are Madhḥij and Māʾkul."""
"3542",""
"3543","Mahmud ibn Labid reported: When Sa'd the one with kohl was wounded on the day of the Trench, and his condition became serious, they moved him to a woman named Rufaydah, who used to treat the wounded. The Prophet ﷺ, whenever he passed by him, would say: ""How did you spend the evening?"" And when morning came, he would say: ""How did you spend the morning?"" And he would inform him of his condition. Until it was the night in which his people moved him, and his condition worsened, so they carried him to Banu Abd al-Ashhal, to their dwellings. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, as was his custom to ask about him, and they said: ""They have taken him away."" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out, and we went out with him. He hastened his walk until the straps of our sandals broke and our cloaks fell from our necks. His companions complained to him about this: ""O Messenger of Allah! You have exhausted us with walking."" He said: ""I fear that the angels may precede us to him and wash him, just as they washed Hanzalah."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached the house while he was being washed, and his mother was weeping over him, saying:""Woe to your mother, O Sa'd!   His waist-wrapper and his cloak.""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Every wailing woman lies, except the mother of Sa'd."" Then he was carried out. The people—or whoever Allah willed among them—said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We have never carried a dead body lighter upon us than Sa'd."" He said: ""What prevents you from finding him light? Angels have descended in such-and-such numbers."" And he mentioned a great number which I did not memorize. ""They have never descended before their day today; they carried him along with you."""
"3544",""
"3545",""
"3546",""
"3547",""
"3548",""
"3549",""
"3550","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: ""When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken by night to the Farthest Mosque, he awoke and spoke to the people about it. Some of those who had believed in him and accepted him turned back on their heels (apostatized). They went to Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: 'What do you think of your companion? He claims that he was taken by night to Bayt al-Maqdis (Jerusalem).' He said: 'Did he say that?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'If he said that, then he has spoken the truth.' They said: 'Do you believe that he went to Bayt al-Maqdis last night and returned before morning?' He said: 'Yes, indeed I believe him in what is even farther than that; I believe him with the news of the heavens in a single morning or evening.' For that reason, Abū Bakr was named: al-Ṣiddīq (the Truthful) (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"3551",""
"3552",""
"3553",""
"3554",""
"3555","Anas ibn Malik was asked about the dyeing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not have gray hair except a little, but Abu Bakr and Umar after him dyed with henna and katam."" He said: ""Abu Bakr brought his father Abu Quhafa to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of the Conquest of Mecca, carrying him until he placed him before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Bakr: 'If you had left the old man, we would have come to him'—as an honor for Abu Bakr. So he embraced Islam, and his beard and head were like thaghama in whiteness. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Change them and avoid black.'"""
"3556",""
"3557",""
"3558",""
"3559",""
"3560",""
"3561",""
"3562",""
"3563",""
"3564",""
"3565","'Aqil ibn Abi Talib said: Quraysh came to Abu Talib and said, ""Have you seen Ahmad? He harms us in our gathering place and in our mosque, so forbid him from that."" He said, ""O 'Aqil, bring me Muhammad."" So I went and brought him. He said, ""O son of my brother! Your paternal uncles claim that you harm them in their gathering place and in their mosque, so desist from that."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ glanced with his sight toward the sky (and in another narration: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned his sight toward the sky). He said, ""I am no more able to abandon that for you than you are able to kindle for me a flame from it""—meaning the sun. Abu Talib said, ""My nephew has not lied, so return."""
"3566","On the authority of ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) dispatched an army and appointed ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib over them. He went on the expedition and took a slave girl, so they disapproved of it. Four of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) made a pact, saying: ""If we meet the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), we will inform him of what ʿAlī did."" It was the custom of the Muslims that when they returned from a journey, they would first go to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), greet him, and then return to their dwellings. When the expedition returned, they greeted the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family). One of the four stood up and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Did you not see what ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib did, such and such?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) turned away from him. Then the second stood up and said the same as his statement, so he turned away from him. Then the third stood up and said the same as his statement, so he turned away from him. Then the fourth stood up and said the same as they said. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) turned towards them, and anger was recognizable on his face, and he said: ""What do you want from ʿAlī? Indeed, ʿAlī is from me and I am from him, and he is the guardian of every believer after me."""
"3567",""
"3568",""
"3569",""
"3570",""
"3571","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah, Mother of the Believers, she said: We, the wives of the Prophet (peace be upon him), were all with him, not one of us remained behind. Then Fāṭimah came walking, and by Allah, her gait did not differ from the gait of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). When he saw her, he welcomed her and said: ""Welcome, my daughter."" Then he seated her on his right or on his left. Then he whispered to her, and she wept bitterly. When he saw her grief, he whispered to her a second time, and she laughed. So I said to her, from among his wives: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) singled you out with the secret from among us, then you weep?"" When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) stood up, I asked her: ""What did he whisper to you?"" She said: ""I would not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."" When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) passed away, I said to her: ""I adjure you by the right I have over you to tell me."" She said: ""Now, yes."" So she informed me. She said: ""As for when he whispered to me the first time, he informed me: 'Gabriel used to review the Qurʾān with me once every year, and he has reviewed it with me twice this year, and I do not see the term (of my life) except that it has drawn near. So fear Allah and be patient, for I am an excellent predecessor for you.'"" She said: ""So I wept the weeping you saw. When he saw my distress, he whispered to me a second time and said: 'O Fāṭimah! Would it not please you to be the leader of the women of the believers, or the leader of the women of this nation?' [So I laughed the laughter you saw.]"""
