"3595","On the authority of Khālid ibn Maʿdān, from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, that they said to him: ""Tell us about yourself."" He said: ""Yes, I am the supplication of my father Abraham and the glad tidings of Jesus, peace be upon them both. And my mother saw, when she was pregnant with me, that a light came forth from her which illuminated the palaces of Syria. And I was nursed among the Banū Saʿd ibn Bakr. While I was among some lambs of ours, two men came to me wearing white garments, with a golden basin filled with snow. They laid me down, split open my belly, then took out my heart, split it open, and removed a black clot from it, which they threw away. Then they washed my heart and belly with that snow until they had cleansed it, then returned it to its place. Then one of them said to his companion: 'Weigh him against ten of his ummah.' So they weighed me against ten, and I outweighed them. Then he said: 'Weigh him against a hundred of his ummah.' So they weighed me against a hundred, and I outweighed them. Then he said: 'Weigh him against a thousand of his ummah.' So they weighed me against a thousand, and I outweighed them. He said: 'Leave him, for if you weighed him against his entire ummah, he would outweigh them.'"""
